---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Spidergraph — Incident Response Card"
  description="Build your own printable incident-response wallet card: bank, card, and carrier fraud lines plus the first three things to do under pressure."
  path="incident-response-card/"
  current="incident-response"
  accent="amber"
  noPrint={true}
>
  <link
    slot="head"
    rel="stylesheet"
    href={`${base}pages/incident-response-card.css`}
  />

  <div class="wrap no-print">
    <header>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Quick reference · Incident Response Runbooks</div>
        <h1>
          Incident Response <span>Card</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="sub">
          Fill in your own fraud lines once, then print or save the card — three
          steps and four numbers, ready before you need them under pressure.
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="resetBtn">
        Reset card
      </button>
    </header>

    <div class="intro-card">
      <b>Why this exists:</b> the Recommendations Report describes a "15-minute
      runbook... taped somewhere" as more useful mid-incident than a document
      you have to search through. This builds that card from your own numbers
      instead of leaving it as a paragraph to act on later.
      <div class="links">
        <a href="../playbook/#incident-response-runbooks">
          📖 Read the full runbooks in the Playbook →
        </a>
        <a href="../digital-legacy-worksheet/">📋 Digital Legacy Worksheet →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="layout">
      <div>
        <div class="form-card">
          <div class="form-card-title">Your fraud &amp; support lines</div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="bankLine">Bank fraud line</label>
            <input
              type="tel"
              id="bankLine"
              placeholder="Number on the back of your card or bank's official site"
              maxlength="60"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="cardLine">Card issuer fraud line</label>
            <input
              type="tel"
              id="cardLine"
              placeholder="If different from your bank"
              maxlength="60"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="carrierLine">Mobile carrier fraud/support line</label>
            <input
              type="tel"
              id="carrierLine"
              placeholder="For SIM-swap attempts"
              maxlength="60"
            />
            <span class="hint">
              Runbook C in the Playbook covers what to do the moment a SIM swap
              is suspected.
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="policeLine">Non-emergency police line</label>
            <input
              type="tel"
              id="policeLine"
              placeholder="Local non-emergency number"
              maxlength="60"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="note">Optional note</label>
            <textarea
              id="note"
              placeholder="e.g. email recovery phone is on file with carrier; password manager emergency contact is..."
              maxlength="300"
            ></textarea>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-card">
          <div class="form-card-title">First 15 minutes (from Runbook A)</div>
          <ol class="runbook">
            <li>
              <span class="step-num">1</span>
              <span>
                Change the password on the affected account from a known-clean
                device. If it's email, do this first — email is the recovery
                path for everything else.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="step-num">2</span>
              <span>Revoke all active sessions/devices on the account.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="step-num">3</span>
              <span>
                Check recovery email/phone for tampering before doing anything
                else.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Completeness</div>
          <div class="score-row">
            <div>
              <div class="score-num" id="scoreNum">
                0/4
              </div>
              <div class="score-label">numbers filled in</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="save-indicator" id="saveIndicator"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Get the card</div>
          <div class="btn-stack">
            <button type="button" id="printBtn">
              Print card 🖨
            </button>
            <button type="button" id="exportBtn" class="reset-btn">
              Export as text ↓
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Companion tool</div>
          <p class="small">
            Who calls on your behalf if you can't is a different question — see
            the Digital Legacy Worksheet.
          </p>
          <a class="card-link" href="../digital-legacy-worksheet/">
            Digital Legacy Worksheet →
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">History</div>
          <p class="small">
            Save a dated checkpoint to compare completeness over time.
          </p>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="snapshotBtn"
            class="reset-btn"
            style="width:100%; margin-bottom:12px;"
          >
            Save snapshot
          </button>
          <div id="historyList" class="history-list"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <b>Companion pages:</b> the full Detect → Contain → Eradicate → Recover
      runbooks live in the <b>Playbook</b>. Everything you type here stays in
      this browser only, in <code>localStorage</code> — nothing is sent
      anywhere, and printing happens entirely on your own device.
    </footer>
  </div>

  <div id="printCard" class="print-card">
    <div class="print-card-title">SPIDERGRAPH — INCIDENT RESPONSE CARD</div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>1.</b> Change password from a clean device (email first).
    </div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>2.</b> Revoke all active sessions/devices.
    </div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>3.</b> Check recovery email/phone for tampering.
    </div>
    <hr />
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>Bank fraud line:</b>
      <span id="pBank">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>Card fraud line:</b>
      <span id="pCard">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>Carrier fraud line:</b>
      <span id="pCarrier">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="print-row">
      <b>Non-emergency police:</b>
      <span id="pPolice">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="print-row" id="pNoteRow" hidden>
      <b>Note:</b>
      <span id="pNote"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src={`${base}shared/persist.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/history.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}pages/incident-response-card.js`} is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
